Z||000009||Robert||07-04-2001||12:56 AM||||Not all that long ago I owned an ’88 GTA, but my wife could not stand the hump in the floor on the passenger side.  I looked at the 2001 TA and it still had the hump.  The salesman said they get a few complaints about the hump, but GM can’t figure out another place to put the converter.  So…….. I bought my “not so average” Mustang, and my wife and I are very happy.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P><BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Mustang_golf-small.jpg"> <P>------------------<BR>           <IMG SRC="http://canterburytrails.com/photo/T2.GIF">  <P> "By the time you die, you should be so used to <BR>paying taxes that it would be almost second nature <BR>to you."<P>Will Rogers, U.S. Writer and Humorist||||reg||10
Z||000010||Slammed Fiero||07-04-2001||01:00 AM||||I just speak from experience<P>Such as<P>Working in GM marketing on Ad campaigns for Pontiac and looking at Raw sales data from 1998 to 1999<P>Working at Condie Pontiac Buick in kingston Ontario selling<P>Working at Kennedy ford in oakville.<P>also having had the oppertunity to have a 1984 Trans am 15th anniversary , white , blue decals , recaro interior , 305.<P>I agree the F body is a monster , I have a Several friends who run them. Fastest F bodies in North america around a track. But there are a lot of reasons that I choose the mustang over the Camaro , I'm a chevy guy at heart , I love the small block. Anyone who has followed my exploits knows we have a Lt4 Caprice wagon done up as an impala SS , we have had a few F bodies over the last 30 years. Personally my favorite was our  (I Firebird with a SOHC inline six , it would out run our 326 firebird 4spd.<P>When it comes down to preference , people make choices for different reasons. I take a car a whole , I know a lot of people that in certian situations buy based on raw performance #'s , the majority of the public is looking to other reasons to buy , hence the mustangs huge sales success. You can look at what cars reside in the junk yard , but that doesn't mean much when it comes to the success of a car.<P>And right now the mustang is outselling the F body by far. Does it mean it's a better car...Dunno ..there is some reason there selling so much , the incentives offered on each car are basically the same.<P>I think we can just agree to disagree. and if a TA beat me , I have a stable full of muscle to back up the little Fiero.<P><BR>   <P>||||reg||1
