Z||000013||Pontiaddict||07-04-2001||02:00 AM||||I've ridden in my friends 2000 Firebird on plenty of occasions and the only problem I've noticed with it is the feeling of rear end sway over bumps caused by the panhard bar. <BR>Another reason besides the ones already noted by others here for the success of the Mustang is it's high(er) rideing seatng position and it's more of an SUV feel to it compared to a F-body. Plus a small family can actually fit 3 kids in the back seat. The Mustang simply is more practical than the f-body. I don't need a practical car, so I still choose the Trans Am. Though if it were me, I'd go with a Formula WS6 non ramair hood (if it's still an option and not standard in that package) pewter metallic paint.<BR>Despite what everyone else thinks about the future of the f-body, I believe that it's still going to be produced. But look for it to be more practical like the Mustang, though still capable of kicking it's butt in a stoplight grudge match.||||reg||1
