Z||000015||Slammed Fiero||07-04-2001||11:09 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Pontiaddict:<BR><B>future of the f-body, I believe that it's still going to be produced. But look for it to be more practical like the Mustang, though still capable of kicking it's butt in a stoplight grudge match.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Sorry , the F body is cancelled regaurdless. Did anyone notice they dropped the 6cyl F body this year (or so I hear) The car is a loss leader , it looses money. The plant in St Therese Quebec is slated to produce trucks. This is rught from GM itself and not hear say...this has been in the works for a while<P>They also cancelled the Z06 powered F body as it would be low production and cost more than it's worth to build. As well the FWD v8 impala will never see the light of day (was suppose to be a fwd all aluminum 5.3)<P><BR>Sorry guys<P>JM <P>||||reg||1
Z||000016||Formula88||07-04-2001||11:42 AM||||Man, Muscrat better than TA?  Slammed, I don't see how.  I rented a v6 Mustang when my Grand Am was in the shop (2000 Mustang vs my 1999 3400 v6 Grand Am).  Hell, my Grand Am felt much more solid, handled better and had more power, not to mention more room.  I can't see the GT or even SVT being much better.  sure, lots more power, and suspension upgrades, but still on that same basic foundation.<P>For my money, it'd be the T/A, hands down.  More money, but more car for the money.||||reg||6
