Z||000026||Slammed Fiero||07-05-2001||09:30 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Pontiaddict:<BR><B>The car loses money for the reasons that I stated.<BR>I know the St. Therese isn't going to produce cars anymore. Not that it matters. I didn't notice that they quit making v6 cars but if you're going to buy an impractical car, then you might as well go for the sweet LS1.<BR>They aren't making the V8 Impala because it would have to be marketed to teenagers who couldn't afford it.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>The impala's target market is no where near the age of teenager. It's bread and butter is 45 to 60 year olds. The reason for building a V8 impala was to serve the law enforcement community first , then to later offer a SS version that would appeal to 28+ year old buyers.<P>The idea is not profitable for GM to execute, I know there  are several 3.8SC test mules at head office in Detroit as well as Oshawa Ontario.<P>JM <P>||||reg||1
